CommitDate: Sun Oct 11 17:34:33 2026 -0500

    fix(landlock): derive payload toolchain read roots so HOME-resident interpreters start. Addresses QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-17.
    
    A payload interpreter under HOME but outside the fixed home allowlist
    (the harness venv at ~/tools/venv) died Errno 13 at startup through the
    auto-sandbox Landlock tier: the tier is an allowlist, _HOME_READ grants
    only fixed tails (.cargo, .rustup, .nvm, go/pkg/mod, .local/*, shell rc
    and git config), so the venv's pyvenv.cfg read — and, for --copies
    venvs, the interpreter ELF and its base-install stdlib — were denied by
    omission. strace-verified on this host: the pre-fix domain returns
    EACCES on <venv>/pyvenv.cfg and <base>/lib/python3.14 while the same
    reads succeed with the tier disabled.
    
    Fix (root cause, no broad HOME grant, credential set unchanged):
    
    - build_layout grows payload_argv (the standalone loader's
      ``python3 landlock-loader.py -- <cmd> ...`` payload). _toolchain_roots
      derives, read-only: the AS-GIVEN interpreter directory chain (pre-
      symlink-resolution — realpath would follow to /usr and lose the venv
      layout), the nearest ancestor carrying pyvenv.cfg (the venv root),
      that cfg's ``home =`` base-install prefix when it lives under HOME
      (stdlib discovery goes through it), the RESOLVED interpreter's
      directory (a copied ELF under HOME), plus the conventional
      ~/tools and ~/venvs tails when they exist (covering PATH-resolved
      interpreters the argv cannot name, e.g. ``pytest`` via
      ~/tools/venv/bin). Deterministic pure function of (home, argv).
    - Every derived root is dropped when it intersects a credential surface
      in either direction (a venv inside ~/.ssh, or a root that would
      contain one) — _intersects_credential_surface. ~/.ssh, ~/.gnupg,
      ~/.config/terminal-jail, ~/.hermes, ~/.aws, ~/.kube, ~/.docker,
      ~/.password-store etc. stay denied; HOME is never granted; the
      workdir/temp/cache/dev write set and the fail-closed degradation
      contract are byte-identical.
    - Non-loader callers (engine capability-probe child, tests) pass no
      argv and keep the exact pre-change layout.
    
    Tests (plugin/test_landlock.py):
    - kernel RED/GREEN pair, host-conditional with HOST-DEGRADED skips and
      fixture homes under XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (outside the /tmp+/var/tmp write
      grants — under a pytest tmp_path home the QA-17 reads would sit inside
      a write grant and the deny could not be exercised): a domain child is
      DENIED the venv pyvenv.cfg without the derivation (the pre-fix Errno
      13 death) and READ-OK with it, ~/tools data readable, ~/.ssh/id_rsa
      still DENIED. RED proven by reverting landlock.py to HEAD: both
      kernel/derivation tests fail, the pre-fix deny test passes.
    - unit cells: tails granted when present, argv-derived venv+base under
      HOME without any wholesale HOME grant, --copies resolved dir,
      interpreter outside HOME derives nothing, bare PATH command derives
      nothing, venv inside ~/.ssh dropped, loader-argv ``--`` separator
      detection, pyvenv.cfg parse leniency.
    
    Verified: plugin/test_landlock.py 127 passed/1 skipped; full suite
    1939 passed/10 skipped; uvx ruff check . clean; board id guard OK
    (read-only); kernel RED/GREEN and end-to-end loader probes (symlink and
    --copies venvs, base under HOME) run against the real Landlock ABI 8 of
    this host. docs/backend-parity.md (a0) documents the derived grants.
    
